s"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1929, J. M. Barrie gifted Peter Pan rights to a hospital; UK law protects its royalties]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134833127.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1929, J. M. Barrie selflessly granted the rights to Peter Pan, establishing a perpetual source of funding for Great Ormond Street Hospital. The hospital benefits from the story's performances, facilitating care for critically ill children. A unique UK law safeguards this donation, ensuring royalties persist beyond copyright expiry. Barrie's ties to the hospital remain influential, demonstrating the power of literature in sustaining charitable endeavors.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1929-peter-pan-author-j-m-barrie-gave-his-rights-to-a-london-childrens-hospital-97-years-later-the-gift-still-supports-seriously-ill-children-with-uk-royalty-payments-protected-by-a-special-law/articleshow/134833127.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1929-peter-pan-author-j-m-barrie-gave-his-rights-to-a-london-childrens-hospital-97-years-later-the-gift-still-supports-seriously-ill-children-with-uk-royalty-payments-protected-by-a-special-law/articleshow/134833127.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-11T08:00:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134833297,imgsize-1647773.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[James Patterson raised his 2015 school library donation to $1.75m, helping 467 US libraries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134832282.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[James Patterson initially pledged $1.25 million to support US school libraries but increased the donation to $1.75 million. This increase followed an overwhelming response from schools, revealing their pressing needs for resources. A total of 467 libraries benefited from the grants, funding books, technology, and repairs. The American Association of School Librarians recognized Patterson for his advocacy and financial contributions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-james-patterson-pledged-1-25-million-to-us-school-libraries-after-requests-poured-in-he-raised-his-gift-to-1-75-million-helping-467-libraries-fund-books-reading-programmes-and-repairs/articleshow/134832282.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-james-patterson-pledged-1-25-million-to-us-school-libraries-after-requests-poured-in-he-raised-his-gift-to-1-75-million-helping-467-libraries-fund-books-reading-programmes-and-repairs/articleshow/134832282.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-11T07:01:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134832399,imgsize-1238987.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia planted rubber vine in the 1860s; it now covers vast Queensland areas]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134789352.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-planted-rubber-vine-from-madagascar-as-a-garden-ornamental-in-the-1860s-the-climbing-weed-now-reaches-30-metres-and-has-covered-huge-areas-of-queensland/articleshow/134789352.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-planted-rubber-vine-from-madagascar-as-a-garden-ornamental-in-the-1860s-the-climbing-weed-now-reaches-30-metres-and-has-covered-huge-areas-of-queensland/articleshow/134789352.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-11T06:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134789529,imgsize-2032597.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 100-kg green anaconda can disappear beneath Amazonian vegetation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791175.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Green Anacondas in Peru's Amazon rainforest were challenging to locate due to their hidden behavior. Researchers recorded observations across various habitats, mostly in floodplain forests. The snakes were often concealed among logs, submerged vegetation, and other natural cover. Basking conditions were primarily found in rivers and vegetation mats of oxbow lakes. The findings highlight the difficulty in assessing the presence and population trends of these snakes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-100-kg-green-anaconda-can-almost-vanish-in-the-amazon-scientists-found-giant-snakes-hiding-under-logs-leaf-matter-vegetation-and-riverbanks/articleshow/134791175.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-100-kg-green-anaconda-can-almost-vanish-in-the-amazon-scientists-found-giant-snakes-hiding-under-logs-leaf-matter-vegetation-and-riverbanks/articleshow/134791175.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-11T11:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134792364,imgsize-301355.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Family mistook missing Rodin sculpture for a copy; 1892 original sold for $1 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/13473